# Docker And CI Standards

Contents: Principle | Deliberate conventions | Not enabled yet | Dockerfile | Compose | Actions | CI correctness | Destructive commands | Docs

## Principle

- Do not weaken Docker, Compose, CI, or delivery controls to make a workflow easier or CI green.
- Keep builds reproducible and least-privilege. Keep release claims honest.

## Deliberate conventions

Do not change these as a side effect of another task.

- Compose file is `docker-compose.yml` (no `compose.yaml` rename).
- Default image target is `runtime` (`FROM runtime-bookworm AS runtime`). `runtime-distroless` is experimental.
- RustFS `/data` is the named volume `rustfs-data`. A bind mount fails on Docker Desktop and would replace the volume in `docker-compose.delivery.yml`.

```yaml
# BAD
- ./data/rustfs:/data
# GOOD
- rustfs-data:/data
```

## Not enabled yet

Activating any of these needs an explicit decision. Until then, document the gap and make no release-grade claim.

- Base-image digest pinning, multi-arch publishing, SBOM/provenance enforcement, full HIGH/CRITICAL blocking.
- Current scan posture: fixable HIGH/CRITICAL may fail the job; the full baseline is report-only. Image scanning is required before public release-grade claims.
- Exceptions and next steps: `docs/security/docker-hardening-review.md`. Do not copy them here.
- Blue/green is a reference simulation until real target infrastructure exists.

## Dockerfile

- Runtime image runs as non-root, built multi-stage, without build-only tooling.
- `.dockerignore` keeps excluding `.env`, `.env.*`, `.git`, `target`, `data`, `logs`.
- No secrets in `ENV`, `ARG`, labels, layers, or examples. No host-local paths or caches.
- A floating tag needs reason, date, and removal condition next to it or in the hardening review.

## Compose

- Ports bind to `${ANTI_BIND_HOST:-127.0.0.1}`. Do not use `0.0.0.0` without a reviewed deployment profile.
- After port-binding changes, run `scripts/check-compose-local-bindings.sh`.
- Required secrets use `${VAR:?}`. `allowall` authorization is local-demo only.
- Third-party images use an explicit version tag, never `latest`.
- `depends_on` uses `service_healthy` or `service_completed_successfully`. One-shot init services use `restart: "no"`.
- Prefer healthchecks over sleeps.
- New services must appear in the architecture rule; init helpers must serve a documented service.
- No new host ports without a CLI, operator, or health-check need.
- Volumes and test data are disposable unless persistence is documented.

## Actions and Dependabot

- Keep least-privilege `permissions` and concurrency settings.
- Pin third-party actions to full commit SHAs. `actions/checkout` sets `persist-credentials: false`.
- `packages: write` only on publishing jobs. Tag rules (including `:latest`) live in `ci.yml` and `release.yml`; do not restate them.
- fmt, clippy, tests, audit, and coverage run on GitHub-hosted runners.
- After workflow changes, run or note `actionlint` and `zizmor`.
- Release claims match the release workflow.
- Fix Dependabot and audit findings, or record severity and an owner for each exception.

## CI correctness

- CI fails when the checked behavior fails. Do not weaken fmt, clippy, test, audit, coverage, or scan jobs to go green.
- No `|| true` or `continue-on-error` on checks. Best-effort diagnostic collection is allowed (see `stack-tests.yml` log capture, `release.yml` delivery logs); label it as diagnostics.
- A cache miss must still build correctly.

## Destructive commands

Name the data to be deleted and get an explicit yes first.

- `docker compose down -v`: deletes this project's `rustfs-data`. Bind mounts `./data/postgres` and `./logs/rustfs` survive.
- `rm -rf data/postgres`, `logs/rustfs`, `data/<slot>`, `logs/<slot>`, including the reset `docker compose down -v && rm -rf data/postgres`.
- `docker volume rm` of a project volume.
- Host-wide: `docker volume|image|system prune` and unscoped container or image removal.
- `scripts/delivery-sim.sh down <slot> --destroy-data`: deletes that slot's volume, `data/<slot>`, `logs/<slot>`, `.delivery/slots/<slot>.env`, and `.delivery/active-slot*` when they name the slot.
- `docker compose down` without `-v` is the restart path and needs no confirmation.

## Docs

- Distinguish local demo, shared internal, and public deployment profiles. The local stack is not production-ready.
- Rollback and blue/green docs say simulated, manual, or automated.
- Each hardening exception has a next step.
